{
  "arithmetic": "A lower F-box hit for R=m*t is a Type I normal form for the scaled numerator P=p*m. Its denominators ABC, ACH, and PK can all be divided by m exactly when m divides A (equivalently m divides AC). More generally c=gcd(m,A) is the largest removable factor: the same target divisor then lifts from modulus t to c*t and gives a Type I normal form for p*(m/c).",
